            "target_entity_type": "Continent",
            "paragraph": "The vulnerability of trees to these conditions was starkly illustrated during the 2018\u20132019 European droughts, where soil moisture deficits led to biomass reductions of up to 50% (R\u00f6tzer et al., 2021). Our model suggests that without improved permeability, urban trees will remain highly susceptible to such climatic extremes. This is supported by international evidence across diverse climates; for instance, (Rahman et al., 2015) demonstrated that trees in paved pits exhibit significantly reduced transpiration rates and canopy growth compared to those in permeable plots, even in temperate regions like Manchester, UK. Furthermore, high levels of soil sealing in North American cities create a 'recharge deficit' that prevents deep-soil moisture replenishment, rendering trees up to three times more likely to perish during multi-year droughts (Hilbert, et al., 2019).",
